---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { usd, pct } from "../lib/funding.ts";
import reg from "../data/vesting-contracts.json";

/**
 * Forward-looking supply calendar. Provenance is a BADGE ON EACH ROW, never a gate on the
 * page: a reader is better served by many rows with honest marks than by two rows that
 * happen to clear the strictest bar.
 */
const now = Date.now();
const d = (s: string) => Date.parse(s + "T00:00:00Z");
const fmt = (s: string) => new Date(d(s)).toLocaleDateString("en-GB", { day: "numeric", month: "short", year: "numeric", timeZone: "UTC" });
const num = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString("en-US", { maximumFractionDigits: 0 });
const badge = (k: string) => reg.provenanceScale.find((p: any) => p.key === k)!;

const HORIZONS = [7, 30, 90, 365];
const horizon = HORIZONS.includes(Number(new URL(Astro.request.url).searchParams.get("days"))) ? Number(new URL(Astro.request.url).searchParams.get("days")) : 30;

// Forward rows: algorithmic emissions are readable today, so they populate the calendar.
const forward = (reg.emissions as any[]).map((e) => ({
  symbol: e.symbol,
  name: e.name,
  what: `Protocol emission, epoch ${e.miningEpoch}`,
  provenance: e.provenance,
  tokens: e.perDay * horizon,
  perDay: e.perDay,
  shareOfSupply: (e.perDay * horizon) / e.totalSupply,
  contract: e.contract,
  note: e.note,
}));

const vesting = (reg.tokens as any[]).flatMap((t) =>
  t.schedules.map((s: any) => ({ ...s, symbol: t.symbol, supply: t.totalSupply, ended: d(s.end) < now })),
);
const totalVested = vesting.reduce((s: number, r: any) => s + r.amount, 0);

const title = "Token unlock calendar, with provenance on every row";
const description =
  "What unlocks next, how much, and what share of supply — with each row marked contract-verified, project-published or aggregator-sourced, so you know how solid the line is.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Unlocks</h1>
    <p>
      Supply arriving on the market, and — the part nobody else shows — <strong>how solid each
      line is</strong>. Every row carries a provenance mark: read from the contract, published by
      the project, or taken from an aggregator. A date is not a fact just because it is in a table.
    </p>
  </div>

  <form method="GET" class="calc" style="margin-bottom:16px">
    <label>Horizon
      <select name="days">{HORIZONS.map((h) => <option value={h} selected={h === horizon}>{h} days</option>)}</select>
    </label>
    <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Show</button>
  </form>

  <h2 class="section">Arriving in the next {horizon} days</h2>
  {forward.length > 0 ? (
    <div class="panel">
      <table class="tbl">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Token</th><th>Event</th><th class="num">Tokens</th><th class="num">Share of supply</th>
            <th class="num">Days of volume to absorb</th><th>Provenance</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {forward.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="sym">{r.symbol}</td>
              <td>{r.what}<br /><span class="sub">{num(r.perDay)} {r.symbol}/day</span></td>
              <td class="num">{num(r.tokens)}</td>
              <td class="num">{pct(r.shareOfSupply)}</td>
              <td class="num dim" title="Needs a clean traded-volume source for this token">—</td>
              <td><span class:list={["prov", `prov--${r.provenance}`]}>{badge(r.provenance).label}</span></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  ) : (
    <div class="empty"><div class="empty__body"><p class="empty__title">No forward events on file</p></div></div>
  )}

  <div class="verdict verdict--warn">
    <div>
      <b>This calendar is one row long, and the reason is a licence rather than a limitation of
      the idea.</b> The dataset that would fill it is DefiLlama's emissions feed, and
      {" "}<code>api.llama.fi/emissions</code> answers <b>402 Payment Required — "Upgrade to the
      paid API plan"</b>. Their adapters repository is not public, and the one that is carries no
      licence at all, which under default copyright grants nothing. A public storage bucket does
      serve the same data, but reaching for it to route around a 402 is circumventing an access
      control, not accepting an offer. So this is a purchase decision, not an engineering one —
      see <a class="link" href="#filling">what would fill it</a> below.
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section">Days of volume — the column that matters most</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    An unlock is only meaningful against the liquidity that has to absorb it. Ten million tokens
    into a market trading a hundred million a day is noise; the same ten million into a market
    trading two million a day is a week of selling pressure. That ratio is the column above, and
    it is deliberately blank rather than guessed: it needs a traded-volume series for the
    unlocking token, and this site's clean volume source covers
    {" "}<a class="link" href="/funding">the perpetual contracts it lists</a> — which do not yet
    overlap the tokens whose schedules are readable. When they overlap, the column fills.
  </p>

  <h2 class="section">How to read the provenance marks</h2>
  <div class="panel" style="max-width:860px">
    <table class="tbl">
      <thead><tr><th>Mark</th><th>What it means</th><th class="num">Rows</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {reg.provenanceScale.map((p: any) => (
          <tr>
            <td><span class:list={["prov", `prov--${p.key}`]}>{p.label}</span></td>
            <td class="reason">{p.meaning}</td>
            <td class="num">{p.key === "contract" ? forward.length + vesting.length : 0}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="section-note">
    Every row on this page is currently the strongest mark. That is not a boast — it is what
    happens when the weaker sources are unavailable, and it is why the calendar is short.
  </p>

  <h2 class="section">Contract-verified emission detail</h2>
  {(reg.emissions as any[]).map((e) => (
    <>
      <p class="prose">
        <strong>{e.name}</strong> mints on a schedule the contract itself publishes:
        {" "}<code>rate()</code> returns {e.ratePerSecond.toFixed(6)} {e.symbol} per second, which is
        {" "}<strong>{num(e.perDay)} {e.symbol} a day</strong>, held constant until the current
        365-day epoch (number {e.miningEpoch}, began {fmt(e.epochStart)}) ends and the rate steps
        down on-chain. {e.note}
      </p>
      <div class="panel" style="max-width:640px">
        <table class="tbl">
          <thead><tr><th class="num">Horizon</th><th class="num">{e.symbol} emitted</th><th class="num">Share of total supply</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {HORIZONS.map((h) => (
              <tr class={h === horizon ? "is-active" : undefined}>
                <td class="num">{h} days</td>
                <td class="num">{num(e.perDay * h)}</td>
                <td class="num">{pct((e.perDay * h) / e.totalSupply)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="section-note">
        Read from <code class="addr">{e.contract}</code> at block {reg.verifiedBlock.toLocaleString("en-US")} using
        {" "}{e.getters.map((g: string, i: number) => (<><code>{g}</code>{i < e.getters.length - 1 ? ", " : ""}</>))}.
        Available supply {num(e.availableSupply)}, total supply {num(e.totalSupply)}, both read on-chain.
      </p>
    </>
  ))}

  <h2 class="section">Vesting schedules on file</h2>
  <p class="section-note">
    Contract-verified, and all of them finished — the last ended {fmt(vesting.reduce((a: any, b: any) => (d(a.end) > d(b.end) ? a : b)).end)}.
    They stay listed because "the contract says this is complete" is a checkable claim, and it is
    the opposite of what a tracker projecting from announcements would tell you.
  </p>
  <div class="panel">
    <table class="tbl">
      <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Schedule</th><th class="num">Amount</th><th class="num">Share of supply</th><th class="num">Ended</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {vesting.map((r: any) => (
          <tr>
            <td class="sym">{r.symbol}</td>
            <td>{r.label}<br /><code class="addr">{r.contract}</code></td>
            <td class="num">{num(r.amount)}</td>
            <td class="num">{pct(r.amount / r.supply)}</td>
            <td class="num">{fmt(r.end)}</td>
            <td><span class="prov prov--contract">Contract-verified</span></td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="section-note">{num(totalVested)} tokens across {vesting.length} contracts, every figure read on-chain.</p>

  <h2 class="section">Addresses that carry no readable schedule</h2>
  <p class="section-note">Named in project material as allocations, but exposing nothing to read. Listed because the absence is the finding.</p>
  <div class="panel">
    <table class="tbl">
      <thead><tr><th>Address</th><th>Why it has no row above</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {reg.unverified.map((u: any) => (
          <tr>
            <td style="white-space:nowrap">{u.label}<br /><code class="addr">{u.address}</code></td>
            <td class="reason">{u.reason}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section" id="filling">What would fill this calendar</h2>
  <div class="panel" style="max-width:900px">
    <table class="tbl">
      <thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Cost</th><th>What it yields</th><th class="num">Provenance it earns</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>DefiLlama Pro</strong></td>
          <td class="reason">A paid API subscription. Their emissions endpoint is explicitly gated behind it.</td>
          <td class="reason">Several hundred protocols at once, with forward dates. The fastest route by a wide margin.</td>
          <td class="num">Aggregator-sourced</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Manual curation</strong></td>
          <td class="reason">Roughly 10–15 minutes per token to find the primary source and check it, at about a one-in-three hit rate.</td>
          <td class="reason">A short list, strongest where it matters. Around 4–5 hours per six usable rows.</td>
          <td class="num">Project-published</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="is-active">
          <td><strong>Archival RPC</strong></td>
          <td class="reason">An endpoint with unrestricted <code>eth_getLogs</code>. Free providers cap it at 50 blocks, about ten minutes of chain.</td>
          <td class="reason">Every factory-deployed escrow in one pass — the Lido case above and everything shaped like it.</td>
          <td class="num">Contract-verified</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="prose">
    The three are complementary rather than alternatives. Buying the aggregator feed fills the
    calendar immediately at the weakest provenance; the archival endpoint upgrades whichever rows
    are contract-backed to the strongest; curation covers the gap between them. The badge column
    is what makes running all three at once coherent instead of muddled.
  </p>

  <style>
    .prov { display: inline-block; font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 500; padding: 3px 9px; border-radius: var(--r-pill); white-space: nowrap; }
    .prov--contract { background: var(--accent-fill); color: var(--accent); }
    .prov--project { background: var(--surface-3); color: var(--text-dim); }
    .prov--aggregator { background: none; color: var(--text-faint); border: 1px dashed var(--border); }
    .addr { font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--text-faint); background: none; padding: 0; }
    .sub { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-faint); }
    .reason { color: var(--text-dim); white-space: normal; }
    .tbl td { vertical-align: top; }
    h2.section { margin-top: 32px; }
  </style>
</Base>
